# Environment variables for development, integration, and e2e tests.
#
# Copy this file and fill in only the values you need:
#
#     cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Integration tests SKIP (they do not fail) when their key is absent, so
# leaving a value blank simply means "don't run that provider's tests".
# Run them with: task test:integration   (or `go test -run Integration ./...`)


# ─── OpenAI ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# providers/openai, plus the OpenAI-targeted cases in providers/openaicompat.
# Also required by most examples/. Key: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ─── Anthropic ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# providers/anthropic, plus the Anthropic-compat cases in providers/openaicompat.
# Key: https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ─── Google Gemini ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Double-gated: the key alone is not enough. Google integration tests are
# skipped by default because the Gemini API frequently returns 503 "high
# demand" errors that flake CI — set RUN_GOOGLE_INTEGRATION=1 to opt in.
# Key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
RUN_GOOGLE_INTEGRATION=

# ─── AWS Bedrock ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# There is no Bedrock API key: credentials come from the full AWS SDK chain
# (LoadDefaultConfig), so an SSO profile is enough, and the tests skip when the
# chain resolves nothing. With SSO, log in first:
#
#     aws configure list-profiles          # find yours
#     aws sso login --profile <profile>
#
# Set AWS_PROFILE unless you have a [default] profile — an SSO profile that is
# not the default resolves to no credentials otherwise. Set AWS_REGION too: an
# SSO profile's sso_region is the SSO endpoint, not the Bedrock region.
# bedrocktest.TestRegion falls back to us-east-1, so leaving it blank is fine
# and matches CI. us-east-1, us-east-2 and us-west-2 all serve the models the
# tests use.
#
# Note for anyone debugging a ValidationException: the Anthropic models are
# INFERENCE_PROFILE-only, so the bare ID is not invocable and NewModel
# geo-prefixes it ("us." in a us-* region). If the "global." variants come back
# AccessDenied, that is an org service-control policy, not a model-access
# problem — stay on the in-geo profiles.
AWS_PROFILE=
AWS_REGION=
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=

# ─── DeepSeek (OpenAI-compatible provider) ────────────────────────────────────
# Exercises providers/openaicompat against a non-OpenAI backend, including
# reasoning-content mapping. Key: https://platform.deepseek.com/api_keys
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# Overrides; defaults are https://api.deepseek.com and the model each test picks.
DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=
DEEPSEEK_MODEL=

# ─── MCP servers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# tool/mcp Context7 integration tests (the key is forwarded to the stdio server
# as an env var). Key: https://context7.com
CONTEXT7_API_KEY=

# ─── Examples only (not read by the SDK or its tests) ─────────────────────────
# examples/web_research_agent — the web_search tool hits the Tavily API.
# Free tier available: https://app.tavily.com
TAVILY_API_KEY=

# examples/agent_interceptors — "interactive" (default) prompts for tool
# approval; "auto" bypasses the prompts.
HOOKS_MODE=

# examples/web_research_agent — OTLP tracing is opt-in and configured purely
# from the standard OpenTelemetry variables. Tracing stays off unless an
# endpoint is set; _TRACES_ENDPOINT wins over the base endpoint when both are.
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT=
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=Authorization=Bearer <token>
# OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=
